      "type": "SINGLE_CHOICE_MCQ",
      "difficultyBand": "standard",
      "stem": "The position of a body moving along the x-axis is given by x(t) = 2t³ - 9t² + 12t + 5 (in meters). The acceleration of the body when its velocity is momentarily zero is:",
      "options": [
        "±6 m/s²",
        "±12 m/s²",
        "-6 m/s² and +6 m/s²",
        "-12 m/s² and +12 m/s²"
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 2,
      "correctAnswer": "-6 m/s² and +6 m/s²",
      "solution": "Velocity v = dx/dt = 6t² - 18t + 12 = 6(t - 1)(t - 2). v = 0 at t = 1 s and t = 2 s. Acceleration a = dv/dt = 12t - 18. At t = 1 s, a = 12(1) - 18 = -6 m/s². At t = 2 s, a = 12(2) - 18 = +6 m/s².",
